* Developed with AI assistance from Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) -- 17-18 Nov 2026
* pli.pfx -- Enterprise PL/I definition for the prefix-macro framework
* (phase B).  Format as in rexx.pfx; shares src\pfxrexx.src with REXX.
* Sources: Enterprise PL/I for z/OS 6.2 Language Reference (DO and its
* types, SELECT) and Programming Guide (MARGINS), Second Edition,
* December 2025.  See BIBLIOGRAPHY.md.
*
* PL/I differs from the Rexx family in what the look-back needs: a
* statement ends with ";" and runs on until it, with no continuation
* character; comments are /* */ only; a keyword may be followed at once
* by ";" or "(" ("do;", "when(x)").
§lang       PL/I
§macro      PFXPLI
§source     rexx
*
* Keyword case: the templates as written, in lower case as in IBM's
* examples (ASIS); the user may ask for LOWER or UPPER (option
* PFXPLI_CASE / GLOBALV PFX_CASE).
§case       asis
*
* Margins: the IBM default for fixed-length records, MARGINS(2,72);
* (10,100) for variable-length records -- the user may override them
* (option PFXPLI_MARGINS / GLOBALV PFX_MARGINS).  No insert starts left
* of the left margin.
§margins    2 72
* Indentation units: 2, from the statement's start (his ruling, 18 Nov
* 2026: a DO on " demo: proc ...;" goes in column 4, the label's
* column plus 2).
§unit       DO=2 IF=2 label=2 SELECT=1 WHEN=2
*
* Mask for the body lines the macro adds, as for REXX.
§mask       40:/* 70:*/ op:&placeholder
*
* Look-back: which lines don't govern indentation.  A line is continued
* unless it ends with ";".
§comment    /* */
§continue   unless ;
§blank      skip
* A label prefixes a statement: the indent is from the label's column,
* by the statement's keyword.
§label      colon prefix
*
* Indentation after the governing line's keyword.
§opens      DO=DO BEGIN=DO PROC=DO PROCEDURE=DO ELSE=IF IF=IF SELECT=SELECT WHEN=WHEN OTHERWISE=WHEN OTHER=WHEN
§nested     WHEN OTHERWISE
§dedent     WHEN=WHEN
*
* After a line starting with END (at the body's column), the insert
* aligns with the line the END closes (his original intent).
§closes     END
*
* ---- commands ----
§cmd        DO          §min 2  §desc Insert DO group; plain DO is DO; (executed once)
§var        -           §first do;                        §cursor body
§var        FOREVER 1   §first do forever;                §cursor body
§var        WHILE 1     §first do while (&placeholder);   §cursor 10
§var        UNTIL 1     §first do until (&placeholder);   §cursor 10
§var        *           §first do %op;                    §cursor 3
§row        pend=RIC indent=DO
§row        indent=DO text=end;
*
§cmd        IF          §min 2  §desc Insert IF
§first      if &placeholder then do;                      §cursor 3
§row        pend=RIC indent=IF
§row        indent=IF text=end;
§row        text=else do;
§row        pend=RIC indent=IF
§row        indent=IF text=end;
*
§cmd        SELECT      §min 3  §desc Insert SELECT group; with an operand, SELECT (expression)
§var        -           §first select;
§var        *           §first select (%op);
§row        indent=SELECT text=when (&placeholder) do;   §cursor 6
§row        pend=RIC indent=SELECT+WHEN
§row        indent=SELECT+WHEN text=end;
§row        indent=SELECT text=otherwise do;
§row        pend=RIC indent=SELECT+WHEN
§row        indent=SELECT+WHEN text=end;
§row        indent=SELECT text=end;
*
§cmd        WHEN        §min 4  §desc Insert WHEN clause
§first      when (&placeholder) do;                       §cursor 6
§row        pend=RIC indent=WHEN
§row        indent=WHEN text=end;
*
§cmd        OTHERWISE   §min 5  §desc Insert OTHERWISE clause (OTHER is its abbreviation)
§first      otherwise do;                                 §cursor body
§row        pend=RIC indent=WHEN
§row        indent=WHEN text=end;
*
§cmd        ITERATE     §min 4  §desc Insert ITERATE; the cursor is before the ";", for an optional label
§first      iterate;                                      §cursor 7
*
§cmd        LEAVE       §min 3  §desc Insert LEAVE; the cursor is before the ";", for an optional label
§first      leave;                                        §cursor 5
*
§cmd        BEGIN       §min 3  §desc Insert BEGIN block
§first      begin;                                        §cursor body
§row        pend=RIC indent=DO
§row        indent=DO text=end;
*
§cmd        PROCEDURE   §min 4  §desc Insert PROCEDURE; the label is its name
§first      &placeholder: proc;                           §cursor 0
§row        pend=RIC indent=DO
§row        indent=DO text=end &placeholder;
*
* Engine built-ins this language uses (no template): pending and case
* commands. Synonyms are the names the setup registers.
§builtin    .. CLINE RI RIC CLC CUC
§synonym    LOC=CLC UPC=CUC
